body:
For `blue` to be applied to all indices, it needs to be at the top level. Only child indices receive the refinements, not scoped indices. This is therefore by design.

```ts
search.addWidgets([
  instantsearch.widgets.refinementList({
    container: '#color-list',
    attribute: 'color',
  }),
  instantsearch.widgets.index({ indexName: 'products' }).addWidgets([
    instantsearch.widgets.hits({
      container: '#hits-products',
      templates: {
        item: `
        <div>
          <div class="hit-name">
            {{#helpers.highlight}}{ "attribute": "name" }{{/helpers.highlight}} // {{color}}
          </div>
        </div>
      `,
      },
    }),
  ]),
  instantsearch.widgets.index({ indexName: 'banners' }).addWidgets([
    instantsearch.widgets.hits({
      container: '#hits-banners',
      templates: {
        item: `
        <div>
          <div class="hit-name">
            {{#helpers.highlight}}{ "attribute": "name" }{{/helpers.highlight}} // {{color}}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      `,
      },
    }),
  ]),
]);
```
